  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nWith the native dialog element it's possible to disable the close watcher behaviour (by setting closedby=\"none\"), then later on set it to enabled via closedby=\"closerequest\" (or \"any\"). Currently, there's no way to do this with userland closer watchers.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nYou would have to destroy the close watcher and then create a new one, but this breaks the ordering of the close watcher stack and can lead to undesirable behaviour when sending a close request.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nAdding an `enabled` boolean to the close watcher interface which sets an enabled state, which is the return value of the `get enabled state` algorithm.\n\n### Anything else?\n\nPopover's also don't have this ability but for that case manual doesn't create a close watcher, and if you change popover state it closes the popover which avoids this problem.",
